  "question": {
    "text": "The position vectors of the vertices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> of a triangle are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> respectively. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> denotes the length of the angle bisector <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AD</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∠</mo><mi>BAC</mi></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math> is on the line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BC</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> equals :"
  },
